<!--
    kuna infrastructure test: the Listing/xref disassembly tier flag
    (`option listing on|off`, default-OFF), PR1 of the Listing/xref tier.

    The Listing/xref tier (docs/listing-tier-design.md) builds a program-wide
    recursive-descent disassembly model ONLY on the real-ELF bootstrap path,
    never the XML datatest path. PR1 wires the `option listing` flag end to
    end (architecture flag/default/reset/set_kuna_option, KUNA_OPTION_NAMES,
    analysis_pass_enabled, the stages.toml settable row, the AnalysisCtx field)
    but does NOT build the Listing yet (PR2). The flag is therefore INERT: by
    default-OFF, and on the XML path it is unreachable regardless.

    This test proves:
      * `option listing on` PARSES and round-trips (an unknown option would make
        the console error and the second decompile would not run / would differ),
      * flipping it changes NOTHING about the rendered C (default-off parity):
        the same output appears under the default pipeline AND with `listing on`.

    Reuses the GH-558 bytes as a small, deterministic loadable function.

    Source:           int gh558(int x) { if (x LE 8) return 1; return 0; }
    Compiled (as):    cmp $8,%edi ; jg +6 ; mov $1,%eax ; ret ; xor %eax,%eax ; ret
-->
